claims.sentence:
According to Section 5 of the Consumer Protection Act, an unfair trade practice includes:

(i) An unfair contract or unfair trade practice or a restrictive trade practice has been adopted by any trader or service provider;

(ii) Goods bought by a consumer or agreed to be bought suffer from one or more defects;

(iii) Services hired or availed of or agreed to be hired or availed of by a consumer suffer from any deficiency;

(iv) A trader or service provider charges for goods or services at a price exceeding the price fixed by or under any law for the time being in force, if the charge is unjustifiable.

